-1 MOTD~

HELP NEWS for further information.

* For new players type:

HELP RULES        HELP BEGINNERS       HELP SPELLGROUP       HELP GUILDS

Hope you enjoy the game!

- The Imps -

Please type HELP RULES, ignorance of the rules is not an excuse.
Type MOTD to read this again.

See also: NEWS, CHANGES, RULES
~

60 IMOTD~
Welcome Immortal!

Essential reading for new immortals:
  help COMMANDMENTS  - rules governing all immortal conduct
  help JOBS          - duties and responsibilities by immortal level
  help QUESTS        - guidelines for running player quests

Communication:
  immtalk <message>  - talk to the staff (also : <message>)
  wizinfo            - turns the staff notices (logins, deaths, alerts)
                       on or off

Remember: your duty is to serve and improve gameplay for mortals.
Do not use immortal powers to benefit your own mortal characters.

[Hit Return to continue]

See also: MOTD, JOBS, COMMANDMENTS
~

60 JOBS~
What staff do, by trust.  Trust is what every staff command checks: your
level, or the trust you were given when that is higher.  WIZHELP lists
what yours allows, and each command has its own page.  You also do the
jobs of every trust below yours.

  60  Help players and listen to them.  Answer from the help, pass on
      what they report, and never play for them.  IMMTALK talks to
      staff, WIZINFO turns the game's staff notices on or off, and
      WIZINVIS, GOTO and HOLYLIGHT let you go where you are needed.
  62  Keep order and read what players file: REPORTS reads BUG, TYPO and
      IDEA, WARN and JAIL deal with trouble, QFLAG covers somebody on a
      staff quest, MWHERE, OWHERE and PWHERE find things.
  63  Look closer: STAT, SOCKETS, LASTLOG, AT, TRANSFER, FORCE and
      NOCHANNELS.
  64  Run quests and speak to everyone: ANNOUNCE, ECHO, PEACE, FREEZE,
      SWITCH.
  65  Investigate and restore: FINGER, ACTIVITY, PRESTORE (a player's
      saved snapshots), RESETPWD, FIXES, QUESTDIAG, GEARDIAG, LOAD, REPOP,
      MUTE.
  66  Correct characters: SET, RESTORE, ADVANCE, RENAME, PARDON, PURGE,
      HERMIE (places the free healer) and EMPOWER.
  67  FSAVE and NONOTE.
  68  Read the world as built: ALIST, ASTAT, MSHOW, OSHOW, RSHOW, RESETS.
  69  Build: BUILD, the guided builder, and ANEW, MCREATE, OCREATE,
      PLACE, RSAVE and ASAVE.
  70  Implementors: TRUST (up to 70), GRANTPSI, DNS.
  71  Given only by the creator, and outranks every implementor.
  72  The creator: SHUTDOWN, REBOOT, LOG, SNOOP, BAN, ALLOW, WIZLOCK,
      NEWLOCK, DENY, UNDENY and CREATOR.

Rank protects: a command aimed at another member of staff refuses one
whose trust is at least yours (implementors may act on each other).
Read COMMANDMENTS and QUESTS.  The rank pages (MARTYR, AVATAR, DEITY and
the rest) say what each rank was for when the game began.

See also: IMOTD, COMMANDMENTS, QUESTS, WIZHELP
~

60 QUESTS~
The following guidelines apply to all quests run by immortals on ToC:

  - Quests should be fun and accessible to the target audience.
  - Prize items must not be dramatically overpowered for their level.
    Do not load an item more than 4 levels below its normal level
    (e.g. level 5 ogre gauntlets are prohibited).
  - Larger prizes require greater group effort or problem-solving.
  - Announce the quest's start so all players may attend.  ANNOUNCE
    reaches everybody online, from trust 64; below that, ask on IMMTALK
    for somebody who can.
  - Have at least 10 interested players before beginning a quest.
  - A quest never needs a restart: REPOP (trust 65) resets the area you
    stand in.  QFLAG keeps a quester's experience and things safe while
    the quest lasts.
  - Leave a note to immortal summarising the quest and prizes awarded.

These are staff-run quests.  The questmaster's automatic quests and the
day's three dailies are AQUEST.

See also: COMMANDMENTS, JOBS, AQUEST
~
0 HEROQUEST~
Hero quests are no longer run: HEROQUEST, LISTCLUE, RETRIEVED and
ENDQUEST are gone.  Heroes quest like everybody else, with Questor Thews
at the top of the Oak Tree: AQUEST REQUEST for an ordinary quest, AQUEST
DAILY REQUEST for the day's three dailies.

See also: AQUEST, HEROLEVELS
~

0 HEROLEVELS HEROLEVEL HERO HEROES 'HERO LEVELS'~
Hero status is reached at level 51.

  - Experience stops at level 50.  To become a hero, buy the level from
    the questmaster: AQUEST BUY HERO (7000 quest points, 5000 once you
    have remorted).
  - From 51, experience levels you again, up to 54 plus your remorts:
    54 before any remort, 59 after the fifth.  At that cap experience
    no longer counts.
  - REMORT starts a new life at level 3 from the cap.
  - Freddy, the training guru (WALKTO GURU), trades a hero's spare
    experience for practices: EXCHANGE.

Heroes keep questing with the questmaster like everybody else.

See also: REMORT, EXCHANGE, AQUEST, EXPERIENCE
~

62 MARTYR~
Your job is to prove to the Implementors that you are worthy of
advancement to a higher Immortal level, either by running decent quests
(not common place ones), helping the other immortals find bugs, area
creation, and generally staying out of trouble.  You were not given an
immortal to boost your ego, so bragging to players that you have one
will not be looked upon kindly.  At this level you are subject to
deletion at the discretion of the implementors, so don't screw up.
Some players are granted this status for helping the game in the past,
and the above does not entirely apply to them.

See also: JOBS, COMMANDMENTS, QUESTS
~

63 'IMMORTAL RANK'~
Your job is to help new players out.  This does not mean you will give
out information about where stuff is, or what something does, or how to
get somewhere.  You could however tell them to go check out the newbie
train.  It means that if someone is clueless, you can say 'go through the
mud school and read the signs', or 'Well, when I was a newbie, I found it
a good idea to train such and such a skill/spell/attribute, but this is
just my opinion.'  You are not to nursemaid the players.  Only help out
when someone is in need of it.  Also, if someone has a bug to report, go
listen to them.  Getting player input is very important, even if their
opinions or supposed bugs may seem off the wall.  You can also run minor
quests, though you must have at least 10 people wishing to participate.
Read the help file QUESTS for more information.

(Written before WALKTO, the published routes, the Gear Finder and the
help that now tell every player where things are and what they do.  JOBS
says what staff of each trust do now.)

See also: MARTYR, COMMANDMENTS, JOBS
~

64 AVATAR~
Your job is to run quests for the players.  One doesn't have to be run
every day, but once a week at pre-set times, or even random intervals,
would be good.  Having quests livens up the game and is a very important
part of making the game interesting.

See also: 'IMMORTAL RANK', COMMANDMENTS, QUESTS
~

65 ANGEL~
Your job is to socialize with the players.  Don't bother them if they
don't want your company.  Ask questions pertaining to the game, get their
opinions on how things are set up, or if they think something is unfair,
out of balance, or needs changing.  Take their comments with a grain of
salt, as a lot of people are going to say 'this sucks' or 'this is
unfair' or 'I need a spell that kills everything'.  You can also run
quests, and are obligated to assist other immortals running them.  Read
the help on QUESTS.

See also: AVATAR, COMMANDMENTS, QUESTS
~

66 ARCHANGEL ARCH-ANGEL~
Your job is to keep tabs on game balance.  This covers many topics.  Keep
tabs on object stats and whether they should be lowered or increased, or
if something about the object isn't the way it should be.  Discreetly
watch how players go about playing the game.  In most cases do this by
asking if you can follow them around.  In some cases you can follow
without making your presence known, but avoid invading privacy.  Check
stats on mobs to see if they are correct, in your opinion, or if
something needs changing.

See also: ANGEL, COMMANDMENTS, JOBS
~

67 DEMIGODS DEMI-GODS~
Your job is to keep the peace.  This means if someone is being
obnoxious, kindly ask them to stop the annoying behavior.  If they
persist, you can remove their channels until they simmer down.  If they
are a blatant pain, gossiping foul language and such, nochannel them and
dump them in jail.  Jailing is usually only for those players that log
on a level one just to make trouble, not players who spend a lot of time
on the game, though they too can be jailed if the circumstances are
extreme.  Make sure you leave a note concerning the incident.

See also: ARCHANGEL, COMMANDMENTS, JOBS
~

68 DEITY~
Your job is to make sure that all the rules of the game are being
followed.  This includes both mortal and immortal.  You are also
responsible for reimbursements, whether this includes loading a few
items, or doing a complete restore of the character.  Characters that
delete themselves will not be reimbursed 99% of the time; you'll have to
make a judgement call for the other 1% of the cases.  Reimbursed items
that are loaded will be loaded at the level of an existing item in the
game, or the character's level if the object is known to be in that
level range.

Restores now go through PRESTORE and the player snapshots; see
wiki/player-backups.md and wiki/operator-guide.md.

See also: DEMIGODS, COMMANDMENTS, JOBS
~

60 COMMANDMENTS LAWS 'GOD RULES'~
.
                         **********************
                         ** The Rules of ToC **
                         **********************

These bind every member of staff, whatever their trust.  The players'
own rules are RULES.

1)  Never kill a mortal, and never send one -- by TRANSFER, FORCE or a
    spell -- to anything that will.

2)  Never play for a mortal, your own least of all: no tanking, healing,
    restoring, buffing or softening mobiles for them, and no gear, coin,
    experience or quest points they did not earn.  The game helps every
    player the same way -- Hermie's free buffs, WALKTO and the published
    routes, LORE and COMPARE, the website's Gear Finder -- so point
    players to those instead of doing it for them.

3)  Keep your mortals and your staff character apart.  Trust given to a
    mortal is never used for that mortal, and a quarrel your mortal has
    is never settled by your staff character.

4)  Do not undo another member of staff's sanction -- a jail sentence,
    a freeze, NOCHANNELS, a warning -- or overrule them in front of
    players.  Take it to IMMTALK or a note to immortal.

5)  Punish with the least that stops the harm: a word first, then WARN,
    NOCHANNELS or a timed JAIL, then FREEZE.  Say why in a note to
    immortal.  BAN and DENY are the creator's.

6)  Restarts are not yours: SHUTDOWN and REBOOT are the creator's.  A
    deploy warns the players and saves everyone before it restarts.

7)  Put back what a bug or a crash took from the player's own saved
    snapshots (PRESTORE: the whole character, gear, stash or a corpse)
    rather than loading replacements, and never edit a player's file.

8)  What you see stays private.  Your commands are written to the game's
    logs like everyone's; a player's address, password and private words
    are never repeated.

9)  Do not kill shopkeepers, the questmaster or anything else players
    rely on, and leave the black market dealer and the treasure goblin
    to the players who find them.

10) Report a bug you find with BUG, and do not use it.

See also: JOBS, QUESTS, RULES, IMOTD
~

-1 HERBIE ANGEL~
Herbie, the wonder angel, now and then visits whoever in the world is
most hurt and heals them.  He is a kindness, not something to rely on.

See also: HEAL, HERMIE
~

-1 RULES~

These are the rules of ToC.  For other matters, USE COMMON SENSE.

Rules for everything that can be done wrong can't possibly be written,
because some things are just not thought of.  If you get called out
for doing something wrong by the Immortals don't retort with it isn't
against the rules.  USE COMMON SENSE.

Note that all punishments also include confiscation of any items obtained
by breaking a rule.

* Foul and/or abusive language will not be tolerated on ToC, from anyone
  (including gods).  This applies to all public channels and to say and
  emote used in public areas.  On private channels, please respect other
  people and stop using language they tell you they find offensive.

* Sexual harassment of any form will not be tolerated, punishable by
  deletion.  This MUD does not exist for you to belittle others.  It
  exists solely for the entertainment of all.  Violate someone's civil
  rights and you're gone, no exceptions.

* We created this game for your enjoyment.  While we don't like the line
  "your being here is a privilege not a right", your use of the game can
  and will be removed if we so deem it necessary for the good of the MUD.

* Cheating will not be tolerated.  This includes accepting favors from
  gods and exploiting bugs.  If you find a bug, report it (BUG), then do
  not use it.

* If an immortal speaks to you, listen and do as told.  Don't argue, just
  do it.  Immortals have a tough enough job without dealing with bad
  attitudes.

* This is a pKill MUD.  If you decide to become pKillable (see PKILL),
  then live (or die) with that decision.  Any complaints in regards to
  being pKilled will fall upon deaf ears.

* Do not bring aggressive mobs to lower level areas other than the ones
  they belong in.  Charming aggressive mobs and bringing them to Dresden
  is looked on particularly strongly.

See also: PKILL, ARENA, BUG
~
62 PUNISHED~
This space is intended to keep a running list of punishments.
Regularly updating the list will enable us to determine what is a
first/second/third offense and handle it accordingly.

Date           Name(s)            Offense                Punishment
==============================================================================

See also: COMMANDMENTS, RULES

~

-1 NEWS~
For what has changed lately, type CHANGES (CHANGES ALL shows every
entry).  This page is kept as history: the entries below are old and
some no longer describe the game.

Recent (2026)
- DAMAGENUMBERS: each player sees damage numbers by their own setting.
- PARDON (staff) clears one flag at a time -- wanted, excon, pkiller,
  warned, freeze or deny -- and PARDON ALL clears wanted, excon,
  pkiller and warned.  "killer" and "thief" still work as aliases.

History (2024 and earlier)
- Repair vendors quote their price before fixing gear.
- Smite wears a weapon down rather than breaking it at random.  Today a
  weapon breaks only when worn to nothing, and REPAIR prevents that.
- Blinding Fists damage was increased; the Fists of Fury flee chance
  lowered.
- Components scatter around the world again; scribe and concoct recipes
  work.
- Psionics: the awakening odds and messages were changed.  The current
  rules are in HELP PSIONICS.
- The Mud School diploma gives a bonus to your levelling stats.
- You can save at level 1.
- Equipment can be damaged; REPAIR <item> at an armourer or weaponsmith.
- Some races can raise stats past the old maximum of 25, by race and
  magical enhancement.

See also: CHANGES, MOTD
~

-1 LYCANTHROPY~
Lycanthropy is a disease out of legend: on the full moon the afflicted
becomes a were-creature, most often a werewolf, and its bite passes the
curse on.  No cure is known.

It is switched off in the game today.  Nobody can catch it, and a
character who carried it from the old days has it removed at login.

See also: RACES, DEATH
~

-1 WEB~
Times of Chaos is hosted at toc.jeremybean.com on port 9000.

Connect with any MUD client, or via telnet:
  telnet toc.jeremybean.com 9000

The first-party browser client is served separately on port 9001.  Local
installations use http://127.0.0.1:9001/client; the hosted game's is
http://toc.jeremybean.com:9001/client.

For the desktop client with automatic mapping, see help MUDLET.

See also: WEBCLIENT, MUDLET, MAP, HELP, NEWS
~
-1 STORY~
The story of ToC revolves around the diaries of Judicandus Bramsheer,
a scholar who chronicled the tumultuous Times of Chaos that shaped this
world's history.  Read room descriptions carefully as you explore -- many
areas contain fragments of this history woven into their descriptions.

See also: WEB, DIKU, MERC, ROM
~

-1 TAX TAXES~
There is no tax.  Long ago the city of Dresden took half of every gold
coin above a million at each login; that tax no longer exists.  The BANK
pays interest instead.

See also: BANK, GUILDS
~

