-1 ROM~
ROM started in early February 1993, using Merc 1.0 code. In July of 1993,
ROM II was started, eventually replacing the original ROM.  ROM was up for
a little over a year, after which the code (version 2.3) was released,
and various other ROM muds were started, including Rivers of Mud under
a new management (Zump's ROM), at rom.org 9000.

Alander's current project is Athen, the sequel to the ROM code. It can
be found on Rehobaom's Legacy, at hypercube.org 9000.

The following people contributed to the ROM flavor of the merc base code:

Socials --
    Kelsey and Liralen

New, Improved Valhalla --
    Liralen

Puff's new special proc and improved poofin/poofout code --
    Seth

Maps and map shop --
    Ezra, Regnan (Olympus)

Nirvana zone --
    Forstall (mobiles rewritten by Alander)

Mob Factory --
    Pinkfloyd (originally written for ROM, mobiles rewritten by Alander)

Geographically correct Midgaard (tm) --
    Alander

Ideas and playtesting --
    Thousands of dedicated mudders around the world

The New Thalos area was donated by Onivel of Jedi, who was also the originator
of the ASCII flags used in the zone files

Beta testing --
    Ken Blosser, Doug Araya, and Sherene Neil all helped with bugs reports
    and suggestions, saving a lot of headaches

Bug reports --
    Thanks to Shad Muegge, Jerome Despret, Phoenix, Will Hongach,
    Erwin S. Andreasen, Adam Debus and especially Gary Turkington
    (author of the ROM FAQ) for help spotting bugs

ROM 2.4 was developed during my time with Moosehead mud, and the release
shares many of the features I wrote while I was there.  Additional code
was written by Seth Scott (the new poofin/poofout), and many contributions
and ideas from the Merc list were used.  Portions of Rusty's work on
Moosehead also remain.

The new features of 2.4 were largely produced in bull sessions with
Gabrielle Taylor and Brian Moore, without whom this release wouldn't
have happened.  In particular, the new privacy code, furniture, and
wiznet are the results of Gabrielle's ideas.

Changes to the standard diku mob and object format, as well as the changes
to Merc 2.1 source code, were done by Alander over many a late night of
hair-pulling. Hope you enjoy it.

(my apologies if anyone was forgotten in this list)

See also: DIKU, MERC
~

-1 'RACE HELP' 'RACE' 'RACES'~
The races a player can choose:

  Human    no special talents; may be any class
  Dwarf    sturdy; good warriors and clerics
  Elf      quick and clever; good mages and thieves
  Hobbit   small and nimble; good thieves
  Saurian  a reptile people, hard to play well

Race sets your starting stats and how high they can go, and the
experience each level costs.  Monks must be human or dwarf, and
necromancers human or elf.

See also: HUMAN, DWARF, ELF, HOBBIT, SAURIAN, CLASS, STATS
~

-1 DWARF DWARVES~
Dwarves are short, stocky and stubborn: strong and hardy but clumsy,
less clever than humans and wiser.  They make fine warriors and clerics
and poor mages and thieves.

  - Resist magic and disease; vulnerable to drowning.
  - See in the dark (infravision).
  - Born holding BASH.
  - May be monks; not necromancers.

Experience per level is 2000, plus this once for your class and once
more for your guild (monks are in their own guild):

  Mage +200  Cleric +150  Thief +150  Warrior +125  Monk +150

See also: RACES, ELF, HUMAN, HOBBIT, SAURIAN
~

-1 ELF ELVES~
Elves are taller and lighter than humans: less strong and hardy, quicker
in body and mind.  They make superb mages and thieves and fair warriors
and clerics.

  - Resist magic and poison; vulnerable to iron weapons.  They may wear
    and wield anything.
  - See in the dark (infravision).
  - Born holding SNEAK.
  - May be necromancers; not monks.

Experience per level is 2000, plus this once for your class and once
more for your guild (necromancers are in their own guild):

  Mage +100  Cleric +125  Thief +150  Warrior +200  Necromancer +150

See also: RACES, DWARF, HUMAN, HOBBIT, SAURIAN
~

-1 HUMAN HUMANS MAN~
Humans are the most common adventurers: no special talents, but they may
be any class, monk and necromancer included.

  - Train their class's main stat one point higher than other races.
  - Gain one point more than other races from magic and gear that raise
    stats.

Experience per level is 2000 for every class.  A human monk pays 75
more, and 75 more again for the monks' guild; nothing else costs a human
extra.

See also: RACES, DWARF, ELF, HOBBIT, SAURIAN
~

-1 HOBBIT HALFLING~
Hobbits are small, a little shorter than dwarves, with the best
dexterity of any race.

  - Resist poison and disease; vulnerable to wind.
  - Born holding HIDE.
  - Now and then duck under a blow altogether.
  - Cannot be monks or necromancers.

Experience per level is 2000, plus this once for your class and once
more for your guild:

  Mage +200  Cleric +150  Thief +125  Warrior +150

See also: RACES, DWARF, ELF, HUMAN, SAURIAN
~

-1 SAURIAN~
The Saurians came to this world through a great portal when their own
was dying.  It was harsher than this one, and they are a hardy, reptile
people.

  - Immune to poison and resist fire; vulnerable to cold.
  - See in the dark (infravision).
  - Now and then strike with their tail as well.
  - Cannot be monks or necromancers.

Experience per level is 2000, plus this once for your class and once
more for your guild:

  Mage +200  Cleric +150  Thief +250  Warrior +200

See also: RACES, DWARF, ELF, HUMAN, HOBBIT
~

-1 SPELLGROUP~
Spells are bought in groups with GAIN.  Most groups come in versions
for different buyers: full mages or clerics (class and guild the same),
other classes in that guild, and necromancers.

  ATTACK        BEGUILING      BENEDICTIONS   COMBAT
  CREATION      CURATIVE       DETECTION      DRACONIAN
  ELEMENTAL     ENCHANTMENT    ENHANCEMENT    HARMFUL
  HEALING       LIFE-UNDEATH   MALADICTIONS   PROTECTIVE
  TRANSPORT     WEATHERSPELLS  NIGHT VISION   ARCANE STUDIES

Each of those pages names a group's versions.  HELP GROUP <name> -- for
example HELP GROUP GUILD ATTACK -- lists that group's spells and what it
costs you, straight from the game's own table.  GAINLIST shows what you
can buy and from whom.  Each spell's own page gives its level by class.

See also: GAIN, GAINLIST, GROUPS
~

-1 ATTACK~
Attack spells (demonfire, dispel evil, dispel good and more):

  attack         full clerics
  guild attack   others in the clerics' guild

HELP GROUP ATTACK or HELP GROUP GUILD ATTACK lists the spells and what
the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, DEMONFIRE
~

-1 BEGUILING~
Beguiling spells (charm person, sleep, invis):

  beguiling         full mages; adds mass invis
  guild beguiling   others in the mages' guild

HELP GROUP BEGUILING or HELP GROUP GUILD BEGUILING lists the spells and
what the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, CHARM PERSON
~

-1 BENEDICTIONS~
Blessings (bless, calm, holy word, remove curse, aid, mana convert):

  benedictions         full clerics; adds frenzy and raise dead
  guild benedictions   others in the clerics' guild

HELP GROUP BENEDICTIONS or HELP GROUP GUILD BENEDICTIONS lists the
spells and what the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy
and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, BLESS
~

-1 COMBAT~
Mage combat spells (colour spray, fireball, shocking grasp and more):

  combat         full mages; adds acid blast, chain lightning, heat metal
  guild combat   others in the mages' guild

HELP GROUP COMBAT or HELP GROUP GUILD COMBAT lists the spells and what
the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, FIRE SPELLS
~

-1 CREATION~
Creation (continual light, create food, create spring, create water) is
sold to anybody in the clerics' guild.

HELP GROUP CREATION lists the spells and what the group costs you.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, CREATE FOOD
~

-1 CURATIVE~
Curative (cure blindness, cure disease, cure poison, cure nightmare) is
sold to anybody in the clerics' guild.

HELP GROUP CURATIVE lists the spells and what the group costs you.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, CURE NIGHTMARE
~

-1 DETECTION~
Detection (the detect spells, identify, know alignment, locate object)
is sold to anybody in the clerics' or mages' guild.

HELP GROUP DETECTION lists the spells and what the group costs you.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, IDENTIFY
~

-1 DRACONIAN~
Draconian (the five dragon breaths) is sold to full mages only.

HELP GROUP DRACONIAN lists the spells and what the group costs you.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, DRACONIAN SPELLS
~

-1 ELEMENTAL~
Elemental spells (cold, water, wind, light and fire):

  mage elemental     full mages
  cleric elemental   full clerics
  necro elemental    necromancers
  guild elemental    others in the mages' or clerics' guild

HELP GROUP MAGE ELEMENTAL (and so on) lists a version's spells and what
it costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, COLD SPELLS
~

-1 ENCHANTMENT~
Enchantment (enchant item, enchant armor, enchant weapon) is sold to
full mages only.

HELP GROUP ENCHANTMENT lists the spells and what the group costs you.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: ENCHANT ITEM, ENCHANT ARMOR, ENCHANT WEAPON, SPELLGROUP
~

-1 ENHANCEMENT~
Enhancement spells (haste, slow, infravision, mana convert and more):

  enhancement         full mages; adds power gloves, fire shield, frost
                      shield and force sword
  guild enhancement   others in the mages' guild
  necro enhancement   necromancers; with death shroud and force sword

HELP GROUP ENHANCEMENT (and so on) lists a version's spells and what it
costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.  Infravision
alone is also sold as NIGHT VISION.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, NIGHT VISION
~

-1 'NIGHT VISION'~
Night vision holds one spell, infravision.  Any mage, cleric, thief or
warrior can buy it, whatever their guild, from their class guildmaster
in Dresden, who practises the spell too.  Necromancers get infravision in
necro enhancement.

HELP GROUP NIGHT VISION shows what it costs you.

See also: INFRAVISION, ENHANCEMENT, SPELLGROUP, GAIN
~

-1 HARMFUL~
Harmful spells (cause serious, cause critical):

  harmful         full clerics; adds harm
  guild harmful   others in the clerics' guild

HELP GROUP HARMFUL or HELP GROUP GUILD HARMFUL lists the spells and what
the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, CAUSE CRITICAL
~

-1 HEALING~
Healing spells (cure critical, heal):

  healing         full clerics; adds mass healing and divine
                  intervention
  guild healing   others in the clerics' guild

HELP GROUP HEALING or HELP GROUP GUILD HEALING lists the spells and what
the group costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: HEALSPELL, DIVINE INTERVENTION, SPELLGROUP, CURATIVE
~

-1 LIFE-UNDEATH~
Life and undeath is the necromancers' own group: the create undead
spells, energy drain, raise dead, trap the soul, ghostly presence and
haven.  Every necromancer also starts with the NECROMANCY group.

HELP GROUP LIFE & UNDEATH and HELP GROUP NECROMANCY list the spells and
what they cost you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, NECROMANCER, CREATE SKELETON
~

-1 'ARCANE STUDIES'~
Arcane studies holds spells from other classes' groups -- earthquake,
plague, harm, major globe and vortex -- for mages, thieves and warriors
in any guild.  You learn each at the level its own page gives for your
class.  Dawn the Wand Maker sells it.

HELP GROUP ARCANE STUDIES shows what it costs you.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN
~

-1 MALADICTIONS MALADICTION~
Curses and afflictions (blindness, curse, weaken, poison and more):

  mage maladictions     full mages; adds maze
  cleric maladictions   full clerics; adds plague and maze
  guild maladictions    others in the mages' or clerics' guild
  necro maladictions    necromancers; with plague, maze, cause serious

HELP GROUP MAGE MALADICTIONS (and so on) lists a version's spells and
what it costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, BEGUILING
~

-1 PROTECTIVE~
Protective spells (sanctuary, shield, cancellation and more):

  mage protective     full mages
  cleric protective   full clerics; adds mass sanctuary
  necro protective    necromancers; with shroud
  guild protective    others in the mages' or clerics' guild

HELP GROUP MAGE PROTECTIVE (and so on) lists a version's spells and what
it costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, SANCTUARY
~

-1 TRANSPORT TRANSPORTATION~
Travel spells (gate, pass door, summon, teleport and more):

  mage transportation     full mages; with portal and haven
  cleric transportation   full clerics; with portal, haven and word of
                          recall
  necro transportation    necromancers; fly, pass door, earth travel
  guild transportation    others in the mages' or clerics' guild

HELP GROUP MAGE TRANSPORTATION (and so on) lists a version's spells and
what it costs you.  GAINLIST shows what you can buy and from whom.

See also: SPELLGROUP, GAIN, GATE
~

-1 WEATHERSPELLS 'WEATHER GROUP' 'WEATHER SPELLS'~
The weather group (call lightning, control weather, faerie fire, faerie
fog, lightning bolt) is sold to mages, clerics, thieves and warriors in
the mages' or clerics' guild.  Through it a cleric, thief or warrior can
learn lightning bolt, cast with half a mage's dice.

HELP GROUP WEATHER lists it from the game's own table and what it costs
you; GAINLIST shows who sells it.

See also: ELECTRIC SPELLS, CONTROL WEATHER, SPELLGROUP, GAIN
~

0 DAMAGE~
The verb in a combat message tells you how hard a blow landed.  From
least to most:

    miss          wound          MUTILATE       *** DEMOLISH ***
    scratch       maul           DISEMBOWEL     *** DEVASTATE ***
    graze         decimate       DISMEMBER      ^^^ DESTROY ^^^
    hit           devastate      MASSACRE       === OBLITERATE ===
    injure        maim           MANGLE         <<< ERADICATE >>>
                                                >>> ANNIHILATE <<<

    Beyond that: "does UNSPEAKABLE things to".

DAMAGENUMBERS shows the numbers as well.

See also: DAMAGENUMBERS, CONSIDER, WIMPY
~

0 DYING DEATH CORPSE CORPSES~
When you die you wake in the Death Room, just above the Temple altar,
resting, with your spells gone.  Your corpse stays where you fell with
everything you carried; your coin stays with you.  Go back and GET ALL
CORPSE.

  - A death to a monster or to your own doing costs a sixteenth of the
    experience you have earned into your level (a FATALITY, half).  A
    death to another player costs none.
  - Your corpse lasts a week of real time and survives restarts.  When it
    rots, what it held falls to the floor; keys and some items crumble
    sooner.
  - RESURRECTION or RAISE DEAD can return you to your gear.

Who may take from your corpse, or pick it up:
  - you and staff, always;
  - never a monster, a charmed follower or a pet;
  - while you are in the game: anybody grouped with you, and anybody if
    you have typed NOLOOT since you died to give leave (every death takes
    that leave back, so you are protected again);
  - while you are logged out or have lost your link: nobody else at all,
    whatever NOLOOT says;
  - anybody, if you were WANTED: a killer's corpse has no owner, whether
    you stay or log out.  Having PKILL on is not enough -- a player killer
    who is attacked and killed is protected like anyone else.
Hyrule's bound items are yours alone whatever else is allowed (and are
lost if the corpse rots away from you).  Nobody may take anything until
your death has been saved ("still being laid to rest").

See also: NOLOOT, RESURRECTION, RAISE DEAD, PKILL
~

0 EXPERIENCE LEVEL XP~
Experience comes from killing monsters, alone or in a group.  How much a
level costs depends on your race, class and guild (see your race's page).

A kill pays more for a monster above your level and little for one far
below; slaying the other side of your alignment pays a bonus (see
ALIGNMENT); a group shares it by level; monsters with special powers pay
a little more; and every kill varies a little.  Rested experience and
EMPOWER or TITANIC add more.

You lose experience by fleeing, recalling from a fight, to some spells,
and by dying (see DEATH).

See also: SCORE, HEROLEVELS, DEATH, ALIGNMENT
~

-1 GUILDS~
A guild adds a second class's training to your own: a warrior in the
mages' guild learns some magic, for instance.  Full members (a mage in
the mages' guild) get each class's best.

  - Mages, clerics, thieves and warriors may join the mage, cleric, thief
    or warrior guild, once, from level 3 to 6, with Melancholy the guild
    clerk (WALKTO MELANCHOLY; JOIN <guild>, 1 gold).  Joining gives the
    guild's free starting group.
  - Anybody still without a guild on reaching level 6 is put in their
    class's guild, free, with that guild's starting group.
  - Monks and necromancers belong to their own guild and cannot join
    another.
  - Each guild has a hall only members may enter.
  - A guild may raise the experience your levels cost (see your race).

Extra experience per level by race and guild:

             mage guild  cleric guild  thief guild  warrior guild
  dwarf         200          150           150          125
  elf           100          125           150          200
  human           0            0             0            0
  hobbit        200          150           125          150
  saurian       200          150           250          200

The halls, each with its own page: UNIVERSITY OF MAGIC, TEMPLE OF BREAS,
CITADEL OF WAR, HOUSE OF THIEVES, PALMS OF THE CREATOR (monks) and MORGUE
OF DRESDEN (necromancers).  WALKTO UNIVERSITY, BREAS, CITADEL, THIEVES,
PALM or MORGUE leads you to one.
GAINLIST shows what you can buy and where; PRACTICELIST who practises
what you know.

See also: GAINLIST, PRACTICELIST, JOIN, CLASS, REMORT
~


0 TICK~
A tick is the game's heartbeat for regeneration, spell durations and
weather.  It comes about once a minute, anywhere from 40 to 80 seconds.

Areas reset (monsters and items return) every few minutes while nobody
is in them, and about every fifteen minutes while someone is.  Items
lying on the ground are not replaced while anyone is in the area.

See also: FAST HEALING, MEDITATION, REST
~

-1 KEYWORDS~
